School Management System (C++ OOP Practice Project and in the stage of development)

A C++ Console Application built to manage school operations, including student records, user authentication with granular permissions, academic sections, and system navigation.

Note: This project was developed primarily as a practice exercise to solidify Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) fundamentals in C++ and practice file handling using plain text files (.txt) as a lightweight database.

🌟 Key Features & Functional Modules

User Authentication & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):

User login system with username and PIN verification.

Fine-grained permission management using bitwise masks (e.g., Manage Students, Section Control, User Administration).

Admin account guard (prevents accidental deletion of system administrators or currently logged-in sessions).

Student Management System:

Full CRUD support (Create, Read, Update, Delete, Find) for student profiles.

Automatic age and date of birth validation (including leap year handling).

Mauritanian administrative region selection (States & Districts/Moughataa) for birth place classification.

Section assignment based on educational stage (Primary, Middle, or High School).

Academic Section Management:

Dynamic section generation for various stages (Primary: 1AF–6AF, Middle: 1AS–4AS, High School: 5C–7A).

Automated numbering and safety rules when transferring students across sections during deletions.

User Management System:

Add new system users with custom permission flags or full administrative access (Permissions = -1).

View, update, and search active system user credentials.

Flat-File System ("Database"):

Persistence achieved via delimited text files (#//# delimiter).

File data loaded into vectors at runtime and updated back to disk upon changes.

📁 Project Structure

Plaintext

├── ClSchoolmanagementsystem.h / .cpp  # Core application orchestrator & main navigation menus

├── Clstudent.h / .cpp                 # Student management logic & Mauritanian geographical data

├── Clsection.h / .cpp                 # Academic section lifecycle management & rules logic

├── Cluser.h / .cpp                    # User authentication, profiles, and bitwise permission handling

🛠️ Concepts & Technical Highlights

Object-Oriented Programming (OOP): Modular class separation, encapsulation, dynamic data mapping via structs, and separation of concerns.

Bitwise Permissions: Utilizes bitwise OR (|) and AND (&) operations for checking user privileges against predefined permission flags.

File I/O Stream Processing: Utilizes std::fstream, std::stringstream, and custom string-splitting algorithms for parsing text file records.

Input Validation: Built-in safeguards against invalid dates, duplicate student identification numbers (NNI), and non-numeric inputs.

🚀 How to Run?

Prerequisites:

C++11 or higher compatible compiler (GCC, Clang, or MSVC via Visual Studio).

Compilation:
Open a terminal in the project directory and compile using GCC/Clang:

Bash
g++ -std=c++11 ClSchoolmanagementsystem.cpp Clstudent.cpp Clsection.cpp Cluser.cpp main.cpp -o SchoolManagementSystem
Execution:

Bash
./SchoolManagementSystem
